  The \textit{t} glyphs and their variants were extracted from a
  typoglyphs repository derived from the multivolume work
  \textit{Polonia Typographica Saeculi Sedecimi} (published between
  1968 and 1981).  The shapes of some glyphs are difficult to
  interpret because the additional component can be read either as a
  diacritic, an integral part of the glyph shape or as part of a
  ligature with another character.

  Various diacritics used with the letter are also
  difficult to interpret. In the paper we discuss in detail some of
  these problems from the perspective of the Unicode encoding and the
  Junicode font.
